menu "CLI API Configuration"

    config CLI_API_IGNORE_EMPTY_LINES
        bool "Ignore empty lines returned by the console"
        default y
        help
            linenoise() returns NULL when it reads an empty/aborted line —
            this happens routinely on "dumb" terminals (USB Serial JTAG,
            Web Serial) that don't support the escape sequences used to
            distinguish an empty Enter press from EOF/Ctrl+C.

            If enabled (default), cli_run() ignores a NULL line and keeps
            reading. If disabled, cli_run() treats a NULL line as an exit
            condition and returns from the REPL loop.

    choice CLI_API_TERMINAL_MODE
        prompt "Terminal mode"
        default CLI_API_TERMINAL_MODE_AUTO
        help
            Selects whether linenoise runs with line editing (TAB completion,
            hints, UP/DOWN history, cursor movement) or in "dumb" mode
            (plain line input, no escape sequences).

        config CLI_API_TERMINAL_MODE_AUTO
            bool "Auto-detect"
            help
                Probe the terminal at boot with a Device Status Request
                (ESC[5n) and enable line editing only if it answers. On USB
                Serial JTAG the probe is skipped and line editing is always
                enabled, since the host is usually not attached yet at boot.

        config CLI_API_TERMINAL_MODE_LINE_EDITING
            bool "Force line editing"
            help
                Skip the probe and always enable line editing. Use this if
                your terminal supports VT100 escape sequences but does not
                answer the probe in time (Auto falls back to dumb mode).

        config CLI_API_TERMINAL_MODE_DUMB
            bool "Force dumb mode"
            help
                Skip the probe and always use dumb mode. Use this for Web
                Serial pages and other hosts that cannot render VT100 escape
                sequences.
    endchoice

endmenu
